; Tutorial_4_Turn_a_Table_into_a_Workbook.inix -- a spoken walk through BatCon, written for buildTutorials (the format is
; described at the top of Tutorial_0_Overview.inix in the Homer kit's Templates).

[about]
Title=4 - Turn a Table into a Workbook
Intro=A table in CSV, inix or Markdown made an Excel workbook.
Setup=BatCon is open, and a CSV file is at hand.
Homework=Make a workbook from a table of your own.

[step]
Say=Press Alt plus B, Bravo, to browse for the file.
Key=Alt+B
Hear=Browse source dialog
Hear=File name: edit combo

[step]
Say=Choose the file and press Enter. BatCon puts it in Source files and refreshes the list.
Key=Enter
Hear=Source files: edit, quote C colon backslash Data backslash Members dot csv quote

[step]
Say=Alt plus T, then the letter E for Excel, moves to it.
Key=Alt+T
Key=E
Hear=Excel workbook (xlsx)

[step]
Say=Every value goes into the workbook as text, so leading zeros stay, and nothing turns into a formula.

[step]
Say=Enter converts it.
Key=Enter
Hear=1 file converted, 0 skipped, 0 failed.

[step]
Say=What this walk taught: Alt plus B to browse, and a table made a workbook.
